        "username": "livingintruefreedom",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/ec9cab/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-09-12T22:04:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>OK, so I played a few game of wage master. Everytime we played we would get the following cards by turn 2 and in this order. The New Deal (end of turn Even amount HP heros take 3 damage), then Losing to the Odds, then Who are you fighting. This setup makes it impossible to win. Granted we got him to flip and after the shuffles guess what came up in the same order. Then he flipped from his deck 4 waglings. So Game over. From that day forward, we haven't played him because there was no fun in playing him in 3 games. I don't mind hard games, but when you can't win because of 3 cards. I feel this deck needs a errata to prevent truely impossible winning condition.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>P.S. make it so that conditions can be flipped over instead of being destroyed would even it out, not make them indestrucable and make them ongoings that taunt you because you can't get rid of them.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
